  "body": "**What's missing:** the MCP server can add and activate setups (`add_setup`, `activate_setup`), but it can't move an operation into another setup or delete a setup. Both are app commands the GUI uses: `SetOperationSetup` (`crates/app/src/commands/setup.rs`) and `DeleteSetup` (`crates/app/src/commands/setup_delete.rs`). A headless agent that put an op in the wrong setup, or added one setup too many, can only `undo` back to that point and redo the work after it.\n\n**Neighbour that works:** `add_setup` / `activate_setup` (`crates/app/src/mcp/setup_tools.rs`) run `CreateSetup` / `ActivateSetup` through the History.\n\n`DeleteSetup` already refuses a setup that still machines operations, with `'<op>' machines in '<setup>' - move or delete it first`. Over MCP, half of that advice has no tool to follow it.\n\n**Done means:**\n- `set_operation_setup { operation, setup }` runs `SetOperationSetup` through `env.history`. `setup` is a declared setup, or null for the implicit first position. The command keeps the stamp, so the op reads `ok` or `stale` by the staleness law.\n- `delete_setup { name }` runs `DeleteSetup`. It takes the setup's private furniture with it, and one undo restores them.\n- Both return what changed. The commands' refusals come back as tool errors: an unknown op or setup, a move to where the op already is, a setup an op still machines in, and a setup another one is placed relative to.\n- In-process JSON-RPC tests pin it: moving an op between two setups, deleting the emptied setup, undo and redo, and the refusals.\n\nLabels per AGENTS.md for an agent-filed issue: `enhancement`, `P2`, `area:ui`, `source:agent` (this account can't set labels).\n",
